<title>PHILIPPINES: Digitel debuts weaker at 2.80 pesos.</title>
<headline>Digitel debuts weaker at 2.80 pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Telecommunications Phils Inc (Digitel) debuted 20 centavos weaker, trading at 2.80 pesos soon after listing on Wednesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>The telecom company had offered its IPO at 3.00 pesos per share.  </p>
<p>Over ten million shares of Digitel were traded in the first 10 minutes of business following the opening bell.</p>
<p>One broker said the listing was poorly timed given that the market has been vacillating within a narrow range amid a dearth of market moving news.</p>
<p>Digitel is a subsidiary of JG Summit Holdings, the holding company of Chinese-Filipino taipan John Gokongwei.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
